# Deferred, link following

- A catalog wake re-asks all visible links in the project, including ones in scopes that
  didn't change (`project-link-resolver.ts`, `link-resolution-epoch.ts`). Not measured as a
  problem. If it shows up in long chats or documents, scope the invalidation to the woken
  catalog's identities.
- Folder chips open their menu only where a folder-menu host is mounted. In other Markdown
  surfaces, such as `TextViewer` and the model-request inspector, a folder chip does nothing on
  click. Mount the host there, or render those chips as plain links.
- A transcript folder chip's context menu shows only its title and address, with no action. Add
  "Open folder" so the keyboard path matches clicking (`rich-content/TranscriptReference.tsx`).
